---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Note from "../components/Note.astro";
import { issue, repoFile } from "../lib/links";
---
<Base title="Features" description="What ACT does around AI coding agents: risk levels, independent review, verification, completion records and the merge that stays with you.">
  <PageHead title="Features" lede="What ACT enforces around the agents, and what your repository settings enforce." />
  <Section id="coming" title="What comes here">
    <Fragment slot="note">Step 7 of the website, <a href={issue(241)}>#241</a>.</Fragment>
    <p>The controls of the workflow, each with the script or policy file that implements it: risk levels and workflow profiles, the reviewer of another provider, verification evidence, the completion gate, triage, and the run records.</p>
    <Note title="Until then">
      <p>The commands and settings are in <a href={repoFile("docs/development.md")}><code>docs/development.md</code></a>.</p>
    </Note>
  </Section>
</Base>
